# Responsive includes a tablet

When shipping or editing a screen layout, check a phone, a tablet, and a desktop. A tablet is the size between a phone and a laptop, such as an iPad.

## Widths

- Phone: about 375px wide
- Tablet: about 768px wide, then about 1024px wide
- Desktop: about 1280px wide

## Do

- Look at each of those widths before calling the layout done.
- At a tablet width, include the side panel if this app shows one there. The content column is narrower than the window.
- Fix clipping, overlap, and columns that only fit when the window is a laptop.

## Do not

- Treat "responsive" as two checks: 375 and 1280.
- Assume a layout that works on a phone and a laptop also works on a tablet.
